---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const base='/equipment/15-09/', manual='https://www.slu.edu/medicine/medical-education/graduate-programs/biomedical-sciences/molecular-microbiology-immunology/-pdf/ivis-spectrum-manual.pdf', lab='https://voices.uchicago.edu/isairr/files/2025/11/Screenshot-2025-11-10-144852.jpg', photo='https://cdn.labx.com/v2/images/catalog/product/4897517/8127ac9e-59f2-4240-91ce-138445169118.webp';
---
<Layout pageTitle="IVIS Spectrum · sealed classic exterior and digital patterns" description="Orbit the closed classic IVIS Spectrum and inspect independently authored grayscale code patterns." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment iv"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/15-09/">← Equipment 15-09</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#iv-evidence">References and verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">15-09 · CLOSED DOCUMENTARY CABINET & DETACHED PATTERNS / FIRST PASS</span><h2>IVIS Spectrum</h2><p>Orbit the classic sealed Spectrum exterior. On the unrelated teaching monitor, see how moving gray stripes can change an image without changing its histogram. A second case illustrates what it means for pixels to be assigned the lowest or highest 8-bit code.</p></header>
<div class="grid"><section><h3>Classic non-CT sealed cabinet</h3><div id="iv-view" aria-label="Orbitable stationary dark IVIS Spectrum cabinet with domed top, fixed front door and separate teaching monitor"></div>
<div class="bar"><button data-iv-view="overall">Reset view</button><button data-iv-view="shell">Exterior detail</button><button data-iv-view="display">Detached monitor</button><button id="iv-cycle">Next digital pattern</button></div>
<p id="iv-ready" role="status">Loading metric model…</p><p>Drag to orbit and pinch or scroll to zoom. The teal badge switches only the separate teaching display. The case has no movable or operable parts.</p></section>
<section><h3>Detached digital pattern comparison</h3><canvas id="iv-plot" width="660" height="426" aria-label="Authored grayscale bars beside a 256-bin digital code histogram"></canvas>
<div class="fields"><label>Fixed digital pattern<select id="iv-case"><option value="stripe">Three gray stripes</option><option value="reordered">Same stripes in a different order</option><option value="endpoints">Code-range endpoints</option><option value="flat">Uniform image</option></select></label></div>
<div class="bar"><button class="primary" id="iv-inspect">Inspect digital codes</button><button id="iv-reset">Reset</button></div><p id="iv-status" aria-live="polite">Choose a fixed image and inspect its integer codes.</p><output id="iv-result"></output><div class="bar"><button id="iv-json" disabled>Inspection JSON</button><button id="iv-png" disabled>Raw pattern PNG</button></div></section></div>
<section id="iv-evidence"><h3>Geometry and evidence</h3><p>Selected configuration: the classic IVIS Spectrum cabinet from the Caliper/PerkinElmer era, not SpectrumCT or Spectrum 2. The <a href={manual+'#page=27'}>manufacturer hardware manual, §5.6</a>, mirrored by Saint Louis University, gives 65 × 77 × 211 cm (width × depth × height). The <a href={lab}>University of Chicago installation photo</a> and <a href={photo}>closed opposite-quarter photograph</a> document the graphite upright case, upper dome, silver handle and casters. Local curves, rear surfacing, trim and fasteners are image estimates. The device is sealed; no optical or mechanical path is represented.</p>
<div class="grid"><figure><img width="660" height="440" src={base+'front.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original metric render of a black upright cabinet and separate classroom monitor"/><figcaption>Original whole-cabinet render, not a photograph. Compared with the installed classic Spectrum appearance.</figcaption></figure><figure><img width="660" height="440" src={base+'detail.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original close-up of the dome, front door silhouette and metallic handle"/><figcaption>Original upper detail. The fixed handle and closed dome are exterior surfaces only.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Independent reference</th><th>Actual / interpretation</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Classic closed exterior</td><td>650 W × 770 D × 2,110 H mm</td><td>Verified metric GLB envelope; separate monitor excluded.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Gray stripe chart</td><td>512 each of 32, 96 and 160</td><td>Mean 96.000, population deviation 52.255781 codes; reordering leaves histogram exactly unchanged.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Endpoint / flat chart</td><td>512 codes at 0, 512 at 255; uniform chart all 117</td><td>1,024 endpoint pixels in the authored endpoint chart. Uniform deviation is 0. Endpoints are not evidence of physical clipping.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Original register acceptance</td><td>Physical dark-corrected signal rate under paired exposures</td><td>Not implemented or run. No optics, acquisition, tissue, camera settings, exposure or processed measurements.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>The detached image is a fixed 48 × 32 matrix of authored integer codes. The viewer counts each value from 0 to 255, computes the mean and population standard deviation with equal pixel weights, and keeps histogram occupancy separate from any physical interpretation. JSON includes the exact codes, histogram and source provenance; PNG exports the authored grayscale pattern only. Nothing commands, reads, or configures a real or simulated device.</p>
<p><a href={base+'ivis-spectrum-static.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={base+'model.py'} download>Editable Blender generator</a> · <a href={base+'pattern-example.json'}>Output schema example</a> · <a href={base+'verification.json'}>Verification</a> · <a href={base+'xr-manifest.json'}>VR action contract</a>. No headset or live hardware was tested.</p></section>
</article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/15-09/browser.mjs';</script>
<style>
.iv{max-width:76rem}.iv .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1.1rem}.iv section{border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem 0;margin:.8rem 0;min-width:0}.iv .bar{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.44rem;margin:.55rem 0}.iv .fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.48rem}.iv label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.2rem;font-size:.92rem}.iv input,.iv select,.iv button{font:inherit;color:var(--text);background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:.14rem;max-width:100%;min-width:0;min-height:2.4em;padding:.32em .52em}.iv button{cursor:pointer}.iv button:disabled{opacity:.52;cursor:default}.iv .primary{color:white;background:#245350}.iv #iv-view{height:clamp(270px,31vw,435px);background:#d9dddf;touch-action:none}.iv #iv-view :global(canvas){width:100%;height:100%;display:block}.iv #iv-plot,.iv img{width:100%;height:auto}.iv #iv-result{display:block;white-space:pre-line;margin:.45rem 0;font:1rem monospace}.iv #iv-status.error{color:#a54a34}.iv .scroll{overflow:auto}.iv table{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.89rem}.iv td,.iv th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);text-align:left;padding:.45rem}.iv figure{margin:.8rem 0}@media(max-width:800px){.iv .grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
